 "policy_menu": [
  {
   "doc": "Emit each accepted detection at once, and nothing else (the historical relay).",
   "name": "immediate",
   "parameters": {}
  },
  {
   "doc": "Full table broadcast on a fixed clock: every ``interval`` steps, everything known. Slots are keyed to the global step counter, not to when a target was discovered, so the schedule is visible in advance and cannot be tuned per target. Because every slot carries the newest snapshot, a periodic policy also recovers a packet the uplink dropped.",
   "name": "periodic",
   "parameters": {
    "interval": 5
   }
  },
  {
   "doc": "Emit when a fact a robot could act on changed, or when the clock says it is urgent. The event set is fixed here and shared by every event-based arm: a new task (its first emission), a stage transition, a change in the remaining capability requirement, a change in who is on the roster, a progress jump of at least ``progress_threshold``, and a task inside ``urgency_time`` of its deadline. Everything else is held: a packet whose payload would repeat what the last one said carries no information.",
   "name": "event",
   "parameters": {
    "progress_threshold": 0.2,
    "urgency_time": 25.0
   }
  },
  {
   "doc": "Event triggers with a deadline on silence: never hold a change for more than ``max_wait_steps`` steps, and never hold an urgent task for more than ``max_urgent_steps``. The bound is what keeps a rule that \"waits for something worth saying\" from becoming an occupancy lease on a robot's knowledge: an emergency can only be hidden for a declared number of steps, so the worst case stays analysable without the policy being lucky.",
   "name": "event_maxwait",
   "parameters": {
    "max_urgent_steps": 3,
    "max_wait_steps": 10,
    "progress_threshold": 0.2,
    "urgency_time": 25.0
   }
  }
 ],
